WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.959 --> 00:00:11.150
Hillary Clinton unexpectedly lost the states
of Pennsylvania, Ohio, Michigan, Wisconsin,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.410
and Iowa.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.309
Those are states that have gone Democratic
in past elections.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:17.910
The question is, why did they switch this
time?

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.939
The reasons really, you can look for them
in the “out states” of those regions,

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:26.359
in central and western Pennsylvania, outside
Pittsburgh and Philadelphia, outside Cleveland,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:31.669
Columbus and Cincinnati, Ohio, outside Detroit
and Grand Rapids, Michigan, outside Milwaukee

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:34.260
and Madison, Wisconsin and the whole state
of Iowa.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.899
What hurt Hillary Clinton there?

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:37.511
Number one: the economy.

00:00:37.511 --> 00:00:39.800
These are areas that feel left behind.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.170
Donald Trump appealed to them with his program.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.010
Number two was condescension.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.910
Hillary Clinton called people voting for Trump
"deplorables" and "irredeemables," "implicit

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:50.910
racists."

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.760
That doesn't win you votes.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.970
And the third thing was honesty.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.000
The out states went heavily against Richard
Nixon and the Republicans during Watergate.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.600
They went against Hillary Clinton and her
secret email server and the Democrats in 2016.

